WEBVTT

00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:27.694
- We will now begin a redemption round.
- What?

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:28.904
Are you serious?

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.114
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.

00:00:31.198 --> 00:00:32.533
I'll go with Pixel Cards 3, 7, and 8.

00:00:32.616 --> 00:00:35.410
- That is correct.
- I'd hate to face Ji-min in another game.

00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:37.037
The answer is...

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.539
The answer is...

00:00:38.622 --> 00:00:40.040
I'll go with Pixel Cards 2, 4, and 6.

00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:42.000
I'll go with Pixel Cards 1, 3, and 9.

00:00:42.084 --> 00:00:44.294
- That is correct.
- How is he pulling it off?

00:00:44.378 --> 00:00:46.588
- He beat four people all by himself.
- He's amazing.

00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:50.425
As the winner of the redemption round,
Team KAIST secured a second chance.

00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:54.638
They can rejoin the surviving teams
and compete in Elite League Season 3.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.349
They really made it back from hell.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:05.857
Good luck, guys.

00:01:05.941 --> 00:01:08.277
- Let's do this.
- Good luck to you, too.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.029
- Should we wish the STEM guys good luck?
- Good luck!

00:01:11.113 --> 00:01:12.698
Good luck, everyone.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.616
It's like hearing our own echo.

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:17.035
Pull us through this.

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:19.037
Will do.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:21.999
Oh, what's that?

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.626
I recognize this.
It's a lockbox for phones.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.211
Oh, a lockbox for phones?

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:29.506
It's a phone jail.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:30.841
- A phone jail?
- I see.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.342
Does this button unlock it?

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.596
- Do we put our phones inside?
- Yes.

00:01:36.013 --> 00:01:37.055
Put it inside...

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:40.225
Then, set the timer.

00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:41.435
I'll select one hour.

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:43.145
Mine is locked now.

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:46.273
The case doesn't open
even if I press the button.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:49.067
- Is it really locked?
- Yes, you can't open it now.

00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:52.112
I would've gotten better grades
if I had had this back in high school.

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:53.614
Then, I could've gone to SNU...

00:01:53.697 --> 00:01:56.241
- I could use it now.
- I'd still make it to SNU.

00:01:58.577 --> 00:02:02.456
If I'd had this in my senior year,
I wouldn't have retaken the CSAT.

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:06.209
I had my phone locked away
back when I was studying for the CSAT.

00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:09.796
I could've used such a smart product.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:10.756
GEN-Z'S THROWBACK

00:02:12.174 --> 00:02:13.133
You're an oldie.

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.468
BORN IN 2007, BORN IN 2003

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.804
What do you mean, "oldie"?

00:02:17.888 --> 00:02:19.973
But your tone made you sound like one.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:21.975
I feel pretty nervous today.

00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:24.311
- I do, too.
- What with the revenants...

00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:26.647
- Team KAIST made it back from hell twice.
- Right.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.191
They had 2 Deathmatches
and 1 redemption round...

00:02:29.274 --> 00:02:30.400
Hey, you're right.

00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:32.402
They're as seasoned as you can get.

00:02:32.653 --> 00:02:35.072
Want to know today's good news?

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.741
- That guy who shares your name...
- Yeah?

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.701
- Did he look off?
- He looked off today.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.120
I feel amazing today.

00:02:42.204 --> 00:02:43.622
- You do?
- My off-phase is over.

00:02:44.039 --> 00:02:46.625
- I'm back to my best form.
- That's great.

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:49.044
- No other teams won a second chance.
- I know.

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:51.421
It's all thanks to Jae-han.

00:02:51.505 --> 00:02:54.007
- It's a miraculous opportunity for us.
- For sure.

00:02:54.341 --> 00:02:56.968
I hope we can avoid the Deathmatches
and play fewer games from now on.

00:02:57.052 --> 00:02:58.303
- Hope for the minimum.
- Yes.

00:02:58.387 --> 00:03:01.473
If we keep our current trend up,
we'll be shamed as attention seekers.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:07.145
All teams, please gather
at the main hall for the main match.

00:03:07.229 --> 00:03:08.230
Time for a glow-up.

00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:09.648
- Here we go.
- To glow-up!

00:03:10.941 --> 00:03:12.359
- With a new resolve...
- Exactly.

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:14.069
With a sharper look.

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:16.363
JACKETS FOR THE FINAL 4 TEAMS

00:03:17.948 --> 00:03:19.741
Impress everyone with a swish.

00:03:19.825 --> 00:03:21.118
Just like this?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.788
Just like this?

00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:29.251
Crisp and fine like K-pop idols.

00:03:33.004 --> 00:03:34.589
- All right.
- Okay, let's go.

00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:40.053
- How about a group photo?
- A group photo?

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.975
- Okay.
- Shall we hit every camera?

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.309
Hit all corners?

00:03:46.393 --> 00:03:47.436
V for victory.

00:03:55.402 --> 00:03:57.779
THAT'S IT
FOR THE FINAL 4 CELEBRATION PHOTOS

00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:10.584
Everyone looks nice in the jacket.

00:04:10.876 --> 00:04:12.627
The vibe's noticeably different.

00:04:12.711 --> 00:04:14.296
Our jacket color stands out.

00:04:15.714 --> 00:04:17.507
Elite League Season 3.

00:04:17.591 --> 00:04:19.551
The surviving teams are as follows.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:22.387
Team SNU in Medicine,

00:04:22.471 --> 00:04:24.598
Team SKKU,

00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:27.058
Team SNU in STEM,

00:04:27.142 --> 00:04:30.270
and an additional survivor
from the redemption round,

00:04:30.353 --> 00:04:31.897
Team KAIST.

00:04:32.647 --> 00:04:33.732
Feels like a déjà vu.

00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:34.858
Is it a revenge match?

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.152
We beat them once. We can do it again.

00:04:37.444 --> 00:04:38.820
Exactly.

00:04:39.446 --> 00:04:42.073
Only the strong contenders remain now.

00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:43.658
From this point on,

00:04:43.742 --> 00:04:45.410
you will not team up by divisions.

00:04:48.663 --> 00:04:51.291
We will have a competition
between the individual teams.

00:04:51.374 --> 00:04:53.752
No more teaming up? That's a shame.

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:55.754
Team SKKU is our rival now.

00:04:56.546 --> 00:04:57.923
We have no allies now.

00:04:58.215 --> 00:04:59.633
We won't lose, at any rate.

00:05:00.926 --> 00:05:03.220
Shoot, my nerves are getting to me.

00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:05.514
Today's main match is

00:05:05.597 --> 00:05:08.058
Dilemma of the Mean.

00:05:08.433 --> 00:05:10.727
- Dilemma?
- Dilemma of the Mean?

00:05:11.436 --> 00:05:13.063
- That's a mind game.
- It's a mind game.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.981
In Dilemma of the Mean,

00:05:15.065 --> 00:05:18.068
your task is to win points
with a set of three cards.

00:05:18.485 --> 00:05:20.695
It is a psychological strategy game.

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:26.910
Each round of Dilemma of the Mean
consists of three mini games.

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:29.955
The first one is the Maximum Match.

00:05:30.038 --> 00:05:33.124
Each team will present an equation
with one card undisclosed.

00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:37.838
The team with an equation that yields
the largest result wins one point.

00:05:37.921 --> 00:05:41.132
If multiple teams have the same maximum,

00:05:41.216 --> 00:05:46.346
the point will be awarded to the team
with the second-largest result instead.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.515
- Sounds like a mind game.
- It's a mind game.

00:05:48.598 --> 00:05:51.142
It's an epic psychological warfare.

00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:53.770
The second mini game is the Minimum Match.

00:05:53.854 --> 00:05:57.065
Again, you will present an equation
with one card undisclosed.

00:05:57.148 --> 00:06:01.987
The team with an equation that yields
the smallest result wins one point.

00:06:02.612 --> 00:06:05.699
If multiple teams have the same minimum,

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:10.662
the point will be awarded to the team
with the second-smallest result instead.

00:06:11.621 --> 00:06:12.956
Are negative numbers out?

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:13.874
However,

00:06:14.249 --> 00:06:18.545
the smallest result
should be zero or larger.

00:06:18.628 --> 00:06:21.298
The third mini game is the Mean Match.

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:23.675
Your target number in this game

00:06:23.758 --> 00:06:28.054
is the mean of the winning numbers
from the previous two mini games.

00:06:28.138 --> 00:06:30.515
The team that meets the target
wins two points.

00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:33.101
In this mini game,

00:06:33.184 --> 00:06:36.813
every team shows
all three cards at the same time.

00:06:37.439 --> 00:06:40.609
If two teams' results
match the target mean,

00:06:40.692 --> 00:06:43.528
they will win one point each.

00:06:44.738 --> 00:06:49.200
If more than three teams meet the goal,

00:06:49.284 --> 00:06:52.120
we will proceed to the next round
without awarding points.

00:06:52.203 --> 00:06:53.580
Oh, man.

00:06:53.997 --> 00:06:57.083
If none of the results
meets the target mean,

00:06:57.167 --> 00:07:02.047
the team with the closest number
will receive two points.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.131
Sounds interesting.

00:07:03.465 --> 00:07:07.385
All teams will receive 41 cards,
each with a number from 0 to 40.

00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:10.472
They will also be given three cards
with different arithmetic symbols,

00:07:10.555 --> 00:07:12.098
plus, minus, and multiplication.

00:07:12.182 --> 00:07:15.936
Please use the cards to make an equation

00:07:16.019 --> 00:07:18.980
that has 1 symbol between 2 numbers.

00:07:19.064 --> 00:07:24.361
Once used,
the numbered cards cannot be reused.

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:29.658
But you may reuse the symbol cards
in the upcoming rounds.

00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:35.288
So numbered ones are discarded after use.
This won't be easy.

00:07:35.372 --> 00:07:36.873
We will have six rounds in total.

00:07:36.957 --> 00:07:40.627
The two teams with the fewest total points
will compete in the Deathmatch.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:41.795
If there is a tie,

00:07:41.878 --> 00:07:46.758
the team with the larger sum
from the unused cards wins.

00:07:46.841 --> 00:07:49.469
All teams,
please start discussing your strategies.

00:07:49.552 --> 00:07:51.930
You'll be given 20 minutes.

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:57.644
Okay, I'll get to the bottom of this game.

00:07:57.727 --> 00:07:59.312
Let's close the door first.

00:08:00.605 --> 00:08:02.816
We should give up the mean.

00:08:02.899 --> 00:08:03.733
Here's why.

00:08:03.817 --> 00:08:06.695
We get the mean by dividing the sum
of the minimum and the maximum by two.

00:08:06.778 --> 00:08:07.988
The former will be close to zero,

00:08:08.071 --> 00:08:10.407
so the mean will be
about half of the latter.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.451
Unless we have another times card,
we can't win both the max and the mean.

00:08:13.535 --> 00:08:17.330
If the winning equation
from the Maximum Match is 40 times 39,

00:08:17.414 --> 00:08:19.124
which yields 1,560,

00:08:19.207 --> 00:08:21.543
and the winning equation
from the Minimum Match is 0 times 10,

00:08:21.626 --> 00:08:22.627
which yields zero,

00:08:22.711 --> 00:08:27.048
the mean value is 780,
the maximum divided in half.

00:08:27.132 --> 00:08:30.176
You cannot make an equation
that yields 780

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.929
without an extra multiplication card.

00:08:33.013 --> 00:08:36.307
In other words,
you would need two multiplication cards

00:08:36.391 --> 00:08:39.144
to win both the Maximum Match
and the Mean Match.

00:08:39.227 --> 00:08:41.938
I saw the times card
as the most important one

00:08:42.022 --> 00:08:47.277
because it decided whether we would win
the Maximum Match or the Mean Match.

00:08:47.652 --> 00:08:48.862
If we give up the Mean Match,

00:08:48.945 --> 00:08:51.948
we'll be yielding two points to others
every round.

00:08:52.032 --> 00:08:54.576
No, no one gets anything
if three teams meet the target.

00:08:54.826 --> 00:08:59.831
I think there's a high chance
they'll all go for the Mean Match.

00:09:00.248 --> 00:09:02.208
- I've got a superb idea.
- Hit me.

00:09:02.292 --> 00:09:06.171
In most mind games,
the players must hide their true goal.

00:09:06.254 --> 00:09:08.923
But here, we have to be transparent.

00:09:09.007 --> 00:09:10.300
- Right.
- Basically,

00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:13.386
it's best to go first
in the Minimum Match.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:17.098
When we do, we'll flash them
"zero times blank."

00:09:17.182 --> 00:09:21.478
It is crucial that you make yourself
crystal clear to your opponents.

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:23.897
We can't exactly talk to each other,

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.775
so our two cards
have to send a clear message.

00:09:26.858 --> 00:09:28.526
COMBINATIONS THAT MAKE THE STANCE CLEAR

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:32.113
Our cards should say,
"Try us if you want to tank with us."

00:09:32.197 --> 00:09:37.452
I think we should reserve
the "zero times blank" option if possible.

00:09:37.535 --> 00:09:41.498
If we use that combination,
we can't win that round's Maximum Match.

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:42.832
- That's right.
- Agreed.

00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:45.960
We could be forced to give up
the Maximum Match and the Mean Match.

00:09:46.044 --> 00:09:49.839
The safest option for us is
to save the times card for the Mean Match.

00:09:49.923 --> 00:09:54.344
Suppose we need just one more point
to avoid today's Deathmatch.

00:09:54.719 --> 00:09:56.888
- That's when we'll use this combo.
- I get it.

00:09:56.971 --> 00:09:59.307
Here's another idea.

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.434
Why don't we hold back on the primes?

00:10:01.518 --> 00:10:02.435
I like that.

00:10:02.519 --> 00:10:04.729
We might need them for the Mean Matches.

00:10:04.813 --> 00:10:05.730
For example,

00:10:05.939 --> 00:10:07.857
let's say we have to make 115.

00:10:07.941 --> 00:10:10.527
YOU NEED 2 PRIMES FOR CERTAIN NUMBERS

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.278
Okay, let's try to spare them.

00:10:12.362 --> 00:10:16.658
In the earlier rounds, the other teams are
bound to aim high for the Maximum Matches.

00:10:16.741 --> 00:10:19.661
- Both STEM teams are bold.
- Yes, they would go for them.

00:10:19.744 --> 00:10:20.870
That's for sure.

00:10:20.954 --> 00:10:23.748
- Go for huge numbers?
- I can see Team KAIST doing it.

00:10:23.832 --> 00:10:26.960
- Team KAIST may try it in Round 1.
- They can just go for it.

00:10:27.043 --> 00:10:30.922
Let's say the two STEM teams use
the times card to get a huge number.

00:10:31.005 --> 00:10:34.634
That clearly means one of them
will win the Maximum Match.

00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:38.388
But then they won't be
able to use the times card

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:40.098
for the Mean Match.

00:10:40.181 --> 00:10:43.476
It's rather better for us
if they choose to go bold.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:48.273
We'll need to save our times card
for the Mean Match of Round 1.

00:10:48.356 --> 00:10:50.024
Let's be prudent in Round 1.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.694
The time for strategy meeting is up.

00:10:52.777 --> 00:10:58.241
All teams, please gather
at the main hall for the main match.

00:11:00.201 --> 00:11:03.955
We need the cards out of their sight,
so keep them behind the platform.

00:11:04.247 --> 00:11:05.999
They might see our cards.

00:11:06.082 --> 00:11:08.751
I could block their gaze from here.

00:11:08.835 --> 00:11:10.795
That may be for the better.

00:11:12.297 --> 00:11:17.051
THE COMPETITION IS HEATED
THOUGH THE MATCH HASN'T EVEN BEGUN

00:11:18.845 --> 00:11:22.891
Let us begin the main match,
Dilemma of the Mean.

00:11:22.974 --> 00:11:25.560
Before we continue,
each team will roll a die twice.

00:11:25.643 --> 00:11:27.562
You'll choose the submission order
based on the total,

00:11:27.645 --> 00:11:30.481
from the highest to the lowest.

00:11:33.067 --> 00:11:34.360
Don't touch this, though.

00:11:35.445 --> 00:11:36.446
Not bad.

00:11:36.529 --> 00:11:37.697
It's okay.

00:11:38.615 --> 00:11:42.076
Team SNU in STEM has the largest total.

00:11:42.577 --> 00:11:43.786
We'll go first.

00:11:44.662 --> 00:11:45.997
We'll go last.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.208
We'll go third.

00:11:48.958 --> 00:11:50.710
INITIAL ORDER:
SNU IN STEM, SNU IN MEDICINE, KAIST, SKKU

00:11:50.793 --> 00:11:52.462
THE ORDER WILL ROTATE WITH EACH GAME

00:11:52.879 --> 00:11:56.216
Team SNU in STEM will regret
letting us go third.

00:11:56.299 --> 00:11:57.133
Well, yes.

00:11:57.217 --> 00:11:58.801
But they may have a bright idea

00:11:58.885 --> 00:12:00.470
- and done it on purpose.
- True.

00:12:00.887 --> 00:12:04.557
Do you want to have our cards set up
to show our confidence?

00:12:04.891 --> 00:12:06.809
- That's a strategy, too.
- Yes.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:11.564
We will now begin Round 1
of Dilemma of the Mean.

00:12:12.523 --> 00:12:14.984
Let us begin Maximum Match of Round 1.

00:12:15.068 --> 00:12:18.529
Team SNU in STEM,
please submit your equation.

00:12:20.448 --> 00:12:23.534
DECLARING THEIR INTENT
WITH THE MULTIPLICATION CARD

00:12:23.993 --> 00:12:26.496
I think they went for 40 times 39.

00:12:26.871 --> 00:12:28.248
There they go.

00:12:28.331 --> 00:12:30.375
They'll probably get the point.

00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:32.961
Quick, let's think.
What cards can we throw away?

00:12:33.044 --> 00:12:34.212
Let's not get involved.

00:12:34.671 --> 00:12:37.548
This is a major make-or-break move.

00:12:37.632 --> 00:12:39.050
We can win with our skills.

00:12:39.133 --> 00:12:40.677
IF LEFT UNCHALLENGED,
TEAM SNU IN STEM WINS 1 POINT

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.512
I'm in tip-top shape today.

00:12:43.388 --> 00:12:46.724
Even the die from earlier

00:12:46.808 --> 00:12:48.559
- knew today's our day.
- Agreed.

00:12:48.768 --> 00:12:53.856
The core idea behind "40 times blank"
was to intimidate the opponents

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:57.068
into using the plus card early on.

00:12:57.652 --> 00:12:58.903
This is a bust, anyway.

00:12:58.987 --> 00:13:01.364
- I'm sure they used 40 times 39.
- You bet.

00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:02.865
Let's use smaller numbers.

00:13:02.949 --> 00:13:05.034
- Go for the smallest we can spare.
- Let's do that.

00:13:06.995 --> 00:13:08.288
You have 30 seconds left.

00:13:09.122 --> 00:13:10.873
Everyone is tucking their tails.

00:13:10.957 --> 00:13:13.334
What if their hidden number isn't 39?

00:13:13.668 --> 00:13:15.628
We know them. They're no gamblers.

00:13:15.712 --> 00:13:17.380
Right? I thought so, too.

00:13:19.215 --> 00:13:20.133
Still...

00:13:22.093 --> 00:13:23.845
- Okay with these cards?
- Sure.

00:13:25.096 --> 00:13:27.932
TEAM SKKU USED THE 2 LARGEST NUMBERS

00:13:29.434 --> 00:13:31.894
- Why would they...
- They must think Team SNU in STEM

00:13:31.978 --> 00:13:33.646
- used 40 times 38.
- That must be it.

