00:48:04.715 --> 00:48:06.342
It's three-dimensional Connect Five.

00:48:06.592 --> 00:48:08.803
Oh, shoot. That looks like so much fun.

00:48:08.886 --> 00:48:14.892
The game will be played on a 5-by-5 board.

00:48:14.975 --> 00:48:20.189
Each player will be given five pieces
in either black or white.

00:48:20.272 --> 00:48:21.941
Among the five pieces,

00:48:22.024 --> 00:48:25.653
one immovable piece will be in place
before the game begins.

00:48:25.736 --> 00:48:27.363
When the game begins,

00:48:27.446 --> 00:48:31.158
1-MINUTE DEADLINE
you will take turns to place a piece.

00:48:31.409 --> 00:48:34.078
There are two ways
to place a piece on the board.

00:48:34.453 --> 00:48:35.746
First,

00:48:35.955 --> 00:48:36.997
you can place a piece

00:48:37.081 --> 00:48:40.501
so that its three-cell side
meets the board.

00:48:41.335 --> 00:48:42.503
Second,

00:48:42.586 --> 00:48:46.674
you can place your piece
on top of a piece already on the board.

00:48:46.757 --> 00:48:52.179
Please remember that the one-cell side
must meet the board.

00:48:53.472 --> 00:48:54.682
They can't use the two-cell side.

00:48:54.765 --> 00:48:57.143
- This is out of the option.
- That's right.

00:48:57.393 --> 00:48:58.978
To place your piece above another one,

00:48:59.061 --> 00:49:03.065
you need to find a perch
to fit in the reverse L shape.

00:49:03.441 --> 00:49:05.568
Additionally, you cannot place your piece

00:49:05.651 --> 00:49:08.779
in the highlighted area
until your second turn.

00:49:09.655 --> 00:49:13.451
From the point where all five pieces
of both players are on the board,

00:49:13.909 --> 00:49:17.079
you may start moving your pieces.

00:49:17.788 --> 00:49:22.293
However, if your opponent's piece
is resting on top of yours,

00:49:22.376 --> 00:49:24.295
you cannot move it.

00:49:24.378 --> 00:49:25.754
A stack like this

00:49:25.838 --> 00:49:28.591
can limit your opponent's movement
while securing two cells.

00:49:28.674 --> 00:49:30.759
Yes, you claim two cells.

00:49:30.843 --> 00:49:33.053
