00:51:14.405 --> 00:51:15.698
One, two, three, and four.

00:51:15.781 --> 00:51:17.992
If we claim a corner,
we only have three options.

00:51:18.075 --> 00:51:21.745
It's clear that we must claim the center
when we're going first.

00:51:22.037 --> 00:51:23.539
I think we should try to layer more.

00:51:23.622 --> 00:51:27.084
They become immovable.
The opponent can't move their own piece.

00:51:27.167 --> 00:51:29.336
Laying a piece flat on the board
is disadvantageous--

00:51:29.420 --> 00:51:33.799
We're virtually giving them a chance
to place their piece above it.

00:51:33.882 --> 00:51:35.342
It's better to layer our piece
above another

00:51:35.426 --> 00:51:36.969
because the opponent can't move it.

00:51:37.303 --> 00:51:39.138
You can't cover up the second layer.

00:51:39.221 --> 00:51:41.765
Place a piece flat,
and we gain three cells.

00:51:41.849 --> 00:51:43.642
But place it upright,
and we gain two cells

00:51:43.726 --> 00:51:44.977
while eliminating a cell for them.

00:51:45.060 --> 00:51:47.146
We can move our piece around,
whereas they're stuck.

00:51:47.229 --> 00:51:49.565
Exactly. We can hold them down.

00:51:49.648 --> 00:51:52.443
But placing our piece on top of theirs
might not always be good.

00:51:52.526 --> 00:51:53.444
What if we remove a piece

00:51:53.527 --> 00:51:55.613
and end up completing
a five-cell block for them?

00:51:55.696 --> 00:51:57.781
YOUR OPPONENT WINS

00:51:57.865 --> 00:52:00.618
We have to know what's underneath
before we decide to move a piece.

00:52:01.160 --> 00:52:03.078
Once you grab a piece,
there's no going back.

00:52:03.162 --> 00:52:06.290
Think carefully in advance
because the first layer is invisible.

00:52:06.373 --> 00:52:08.709
It's pretty confusing
when you look at the board this way.

00:52:08.792 --> 00:52:10.085
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE PLAYS TRIAL GAMES

00:52:10.169 --> 00:52:12.630
I think this is a pretty good move.

00:52:12.713 --> 00:52:15.007
ALL PIECES HAVE BEEN PLACED

00:52:15.090 --> 00:52:17.176
We can now move them, right?

00:52:17.259 --> 00:52:19.136
What can I move now? Nothing much.

00:52:19.219 --> 00:52:21.764
Just these three, right?

00:52:21.847 --> 00:52:24.099
There's this term
called zugzwang in chess.

00:52:24.183 --> 00:52:26.268
So basically,

00:52:26.352 --> 00:52:29.355
it's a situation
where all your pieces are engaged.

00:52:29.438 --> 00:52:33.317
No pieces are free to move,
so you end up making a bad move.

00:52:33.400 --> 00:52:36.987
I think we might see a similar moment
in Block Connect Five.

00:52:38.864 --> 00:52:41.116
What's the setup
that will guarantee me a win?

00:52:41.200 --> 00:52:43.160
- That's what I'm trying to find.
- We need it.

00:52:43.243 --> 00:52:44.411
Like the double-three--

00:52:44.495 --> 00:52:47.039
Yes, something
like the double-three in Connect Five...

00:52:47.122 --> 00:52:50.042
- We need to find that ultimate move.
- Exactly.

00:52:50.668 --> 00:52:52.419
We'll probably go second
in Rounds 1 and 3.

00:52:52.503 --> 00:52:55.422
It's as good as fixed.

00:52:55.506 --> 00:52:58.717
- Gang-hyeon and I can take on one each.
- We could do that.

00:52:59.218 --> 00:53:00.302
I'm feeling pretty good.

00:53:00.386 --> 00:53:02.096
- Let's do as you say.
- Okay.

00:53:02.805 --> 00:53:05.683
It's all about not slipping up.
Take time to think it through.

00:53:05.766 --> 00:53:06.684
I trust you.

00:53:06.767 --> 00:53:08.394
Let me have at it.

00:53:08.477 --> 00:53:09.895
ROUND 1: KIM DONG-GEON
ROUND 2: SONG MYEONG-SU

00:53:09.978 --> 00:53:11.355
ROUND 3: KIM GANG-HYEON
ROUND 4: HAN JONG-YUN

00:53:11.438 --> 00:53:12.898
ROUND 1: JOO MIN-SEO
ROUND 2: LEE SEUNG-HYEON

00:53:12.981 --> 00:53:14.316
ROUND 3: HAN SEO-YEON
ROUND 4: KIM MIN-SEOK

00:53:14.775 --> 00:53:17.528
The time for strategy meeting is up.

00:53:17.611 --> 00:53:22.032
Both teams, please gather
at the main hall for the Deathmatch.

00:53:22.116 --> 00:53:23.826
- SNU!
- For independence!

00:53:24.118 --> 00:53:26.245
- Let's go, SNU!
- Let's go, SNU!

00:53:27.329 --> 00:53:28.831
We've got this.

00:53:34.920 --> 00:53:38.215
They'll probably feel uneasy
because we get to go first in Round 1.

00:53:38.298 --> 00:53:41.677
Let's relax.

00:53:41.760 --> 00:53:43.554
Why do I feel like we're going to win?

00:53:43.637 --> 00:53:45.264
You feel like we're going to win?

00:53:45.889 --> 00:53:48.058
Well, I'd say that's just normal

00:53:48.142 --> 00:53:50.018
because we're obviously going to win.

00:53:52.104 --> 00:53:53.522
FIRST-EVER TEAM SNU SHOWDOWN

00:53:54.314 --> 00:53:56.817
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE VS TEAM SNU IN STEM

00:53:57.609 --> 00:54:01.864
We'll now begin Round 1
of the Deathmatch, Block Connect Five.

00:54:02.656 --> 00:54:04.408
Which team will win
the battle of Team SNUs?

00:54:04.491 --> 00:54:08.537
All four members have to battle it out.
We'll see what everyone is made of.

00:54:08.620 --> 00:54:11.415
It will decide which is the true Team SNU.

00:54:11.498 --> 00:54:14.710
Players competing in Round 1
are Team SNU in Medicine's Joo Min-seo

00:54:14.793 --> 00:54:18.213
and Team SNU in STEM's Kim Dong-geon.

00:54:18.297 --> 00:54:20.090
One of them has to bear the dishonor

00:54:20.174 --> 00:54:22.342
of being the first Team SNU
to be eliminated.

00:54:23.469 --> 00:54:24.845
That sounds so crazy.

00:54:24.928 --> 00:54:26.764
What's more, they come in fourth.

00:54:26.847 --> 00:54:28.515
This decides fourth place?

00:54:28.599 --> 00:54:30.392
This is way too intense.

00:54:30.809 --> 00:54:33.812
As Team SNU in Medicine
held a higher rank in the main match,

00:54:33.896 --> 00:54:36.148
their player will decide who goes first.

00:54:36.648 --> 00:54:38.150
We'll go first.

00:54:40.194 --> 00:54:41.737
Are you sure about this?

00:54:41.820 --> 00:54:43.989
Of course.

00:54:46.283 --> 00:54:49.620
I was sure I could beat the disadvantage.
I felt confident going in.

00:54:49.953 --> 00:54:51.747
First player, please place a piece.

00:54:51.830 --> 00:54:53.248
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE'S TURN

00:54:55.167 --> 00:54:57.836
She has to go for the center.

00:55:01.590 --> 00:55:03.217
That's a shocker.

00:55:07.596 --> 00:55:11.517
AGAINST ALL EXPECTATION,
JOO MIN-SEO DIDN'T CLAIM THE CENTER

00:55:11.809 --> 00:55:16.605
My team concluded that the first player
had to take the center at the outset.

00:55:16.688 --> 00:55:19.942
So Min-seo's first move was unexpected.

00:55:20.025 --> 00:55:21.151
It threw me off,

00:55:21.235 --> 00:55:24.112
but I still thought it was important
to take the center.

00:55:33.413 --> 00:55:35.499
JOO MIN-SEO HAS A 4-CELL BLOCK

00:55:35.958 --> 00:55:36.792
Hey, she won.

00:55:38.001 --> 00:55:39.419
What the heck?

00:55:39.753 --> 00:55:41.839
It's basically over, isn't it?

00:55:42.631 --> 00:55:43.590
What?

00:55:43.674 --> 00:55:46.093
- She won.
- We won.

00:55:46.176 --> 00:55:47.511
He didn't come prepared.

00:55:47.970 --> 00:55:48.929
DURING STRATEGY MEETING

00:55:49.012 --> 00:55:50.931
What's the setup
that will guarantee me a win?

00:55:51.014 --> 00:55:53.433
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE FOCUSED
ON FINDING ULTIMATE MOVES

00:55:53.517 --> 00:55:56.645
Because we'd be going first in Round 1...

00:55:56.728 --> 00:55:59.022
We tried to find ways
for the first player to secure victory.

00:55:59.106 --> 00:56:03.527
While searching for the moves
that would allow us to win...

00:56:04.444 --> 00:56:05.571
Hey, the game's over.

00:56:05.654 --> 00:56:06.947
- We start from here, right?
- Yes.

00:56:07.030 --> 00:56:08.365
Let's say...

00:56:08.448 --> 00:56:09.575
We place it like this.

00:56:10.492 --> 00:56:13.620
We learned that it was critical
to claim the 4-by-4 point.

00:56:13.704 --> 00:56:16.039
Let's say we took it on our first move.

00:56:16.331 --> 00:56:18.792
If the opponent didn't defend properly,

00:56:18.876 --> 00:56:23.088
we could complete our five-cell block
with the pieces in the second layer.

00:56:23.422 --> 00:56:27.426
Even if the opponent places a piece
in the first layer as a defense,

00:56:27.509 --> 00:56:30.429
you can place your piece over it
to complete a five-cell block.

00:56:30.512 --> 00:56:31.638
If they don't,

00:56:31.722 --> 00:56:35.642
you can place your piece on the board
to get a five-cell block.

00:56:35.726 --> 00:56:38.770
We now have one way to secure a win.

00:56:38.854 --> 00:56:40.314
We can win with this.

00:56:41.690 --> 00:56:44.318
AS PLANNED,
JOO MIN-SEO CLAIMS THE 4-BY-4 POINT

00:56:44.818 --> 00:56:47.154
THE RED POINT MUST BE DEFENDED

00:56:47.237 --> 00:56:50.490
BUT KIM DONG-GEON DIDN'T GRASP
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE'S STRATEGY

00:56:58.290 --> 00:57:01.084
Shoot, I missed that.

00:57:05.631 --> 00:57:09.551
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE'S 5-CELL BLOCK

00:57:09.635 --> 00:57:13.096
It must've been
a huge surprise to Dong-geon.

00:57:13.180 --> 00:57:15.724
Our plan worked. He didn't see it coming.

00:57:16.099 --> 00:57:20.312
I realized that Team SNU in Medicine
came well-prepared.

00:57:21.021 --> 00:57:25.817
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE: 1,
TEAM SNU IN STEM: 0

00:57:27.361 --> 00:57:29.363
Kudos to your hard work.

00:57:29.780 --> 00:57:31.281
I can't believe I missed that.

00:57:33.200 --> 00:57:35.285
- That was a finisher.
- I know.

00:57:35.911 --> 00:57:36.995
We can win when we go first.

00:57:37.079 --> 00:57:38.246
What do I do?

00:57:38.330 --> 00:57:39.873
- What?
- What should I lead with?

00:57:39.957 --> 00:57:42.209
We have our strategy.

00:57:42.292 --> 00:57:43.669
You can follow the plan.

00:57:44.044 --> 00:57:47.005
That was the fastest defeat on record.

00:57:47.089 --> 00:57:47.923
Dong-geon lost...

00:57:48.006 --> 00:57:49.883
- I can't believe it.
- Me neither.

00:57:49.967 --> 00:57:52.344
- That was a given.
- It was perfect.

00:57:52.427 --> 00:57:54.137
Simply perfect, just as we planned.

00:57:54.221 --> 00:57:55.681
- Good luck.
- Great job.

00:57:56.098 --> 00:57:58.850
We know our strategy best,
so they can't use it against us.

00:57:58.934 --> 00:58:01.353
Of course. We've got this.

00:58:02.145 --> 00:58:03.689
How do we counter that strategy?

00:58:03.772 --> 00:58:05.691
With good defense.

00:58:06.024 --> 00:58:08.068
Good. We won the first round.

00:58:08.151 --> 00:58:10.070
Yes, I bet their morale is crushed.

00:58:13.198 --> 00:58:15.200
Looks like Seung-hyeon is up next.

00:58:16.118 --> 00:58:17.077
It's okay.

00:58:17.577 --> 00:58:18.954
Let's do our thing, okay?

00:58:19.788 --> 00:58:21.707
BLOCK CONNECT FIVE
ROUND 2

00:58:24.501 --> 00:58:27.379
ROUND 2 PLAYER OF TEAM SNU IN STEM
SONG MYEONG-SU

00:58:27.462 --> 00:58:29.589
- You've got this. Get us the win.
- Good luck.

00:58:29.673 --> 00:58:31.591
ROUND 2 PLAYER OF TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE
LEE SEUNG-HYEON

00:58:34.553 --> 00:58:38.807
I saw Seung-hyeon as the best tactician
of Team SNU in Medicine.

00:58:38.890 --> 00:58:42.728
I thought defeating him
would turn the tide in my team's favor.

00:58:42.978 --> 00:58:47.315
As Team SNU in STEM lost Round 1,
their player will decide who goes first.

00:58:47.399 --> 00:58:48.942
TEAM SNU IN STEM

00:58:49.026 --> 00:58:50.318
I'll go first.

00:58:51.403 --> 00:58:52.654
Please place your piece.

00:58:52.738 --> 00:58:53.613
TEAM SNU IN STEM'S TURN

00:58:53.697 --> 00:58:56.950
How would Seung-hyeon react
if Myeong-su used their previous tactic?

00:58:57.034 --> 00:59:00.537
Would he go for a new hack
or nab the center cell?

00:59:01.413 --> 00:59:04.124
I did consider
using the opponent's strategy

00:59:04.207 --> 00:59:06.376
because it was incredible.

00:59:06.918 --> 00:59:08.670
BEFORE ROUND 2
Should I copy their plan?

00:59:08.754 --> 00:59:10.005
- From just now?
- Yes.

00:59:10.088 --> 00:59:12.758
But that's a tool
they know better than we do.

00:59:13.633 --> 00:59:17.596
But it seemed too risky to try
a strategy that I didn't know well.

00:59:17.679 --> 00:59:19.181
So I went with our original plan.

00:59:20.348 --> 00:59:22.392
CLAIMS THE CENTER AS PLANNED

00:59:22.476 --> 00:59:23.852
Nice and easy.

00:59:23.935 --> 00:59:26.354
I don't think we can call it a bad choice.

00:59:32.486 --> 00:59:33.695
You have 30 seconds left.

00:59:33.779 --> 00:59:34.738
Guys.

00:59:35.113 --> 00:59:36.698
How do you defend against this?

00:59:36.990 --> 00:59:39.534
- You get a double-three.
- You can't counter that.

00:59:40.494 --> 00:59:43.955
If Myeong-su places his piece
like the graphic on screen,

00:59:44.039 --> 00:59:46.249
he can get a double-three in his color.

00:59:46.333 --> 00:59:49.252
Regardless of what Seung-hyeon does next,

00:59:49.336 --> 00:59:53.215
Myeong-su can get a five-cell block
no matter what.

01:00:07.104 --> 01:00:09.523
SONG MYEONG-SU PLACES HIS PIECE ELSEWHERE

01:00:10.232 --> 01:00:13.819
I was so relieved
to have narrowly escaped the danger.

01:00:13.902 --> 01:00:15.529
- That would've ended it.
- Sure.

01:00:15.612 --> 01:00:17.864
It's a pity Myeong-su didn't see this.

01:00:19.866 --> 01:00:21.076
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE'S 4-CELL BLOCK

01:00:22.369 --> 01:00:23.578
DEFENDS SUCCESSFULLY

01:00:25.497 --> 01:00:27.374
ATTACKS WITH ANOTHER 4-CELL BLOCK

01:00:28.291 --> 01:00:29.960
Myeong-su should put a piece
on top of his own, no?

01:00:30.043 --> 01:00:31.128
Sure.

01:00:31.211 --> 01:00:32.838
That puts Myeong-su at a disadvantage.

01:00:33.588 --> 01:00:36.091
He lost the edge of going first.

01:00:39.511 --> 01:00:41.012
All right, good job.

01:00:41.096 --> 01:00:43.807
Defense and offense at the same time.
Good call.

01:00:44.057 --> 01:00:46.268
Seung-hyeon has to find a way
to counter it.

01:00:48.728 --> 01:00:50.856
There we go.

01:00:51.606 --> 01:00:53.984
All pieces have been placed.

01:00:54.067 --> 01:00:56.653
Song Myeong-su, please move a piece.

01:01:04.452 --> 01:01:05.912
Leaving the center open?

01:01:05.996 --> 01:01:08.081
He can't do much, can he?

01:01:09.833 --> 01:01:11.334
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE'S 4-CELL BLOCK

01:01:20.844 --> 01:01:23.054
Both of them are running a tight ship.

01:01:23.138 --> 01:01:25.557
They'll have to wait
for the other to mess up.

01:01:27.934 --> 01:01:29.978
BOTH DEFEND WITHOUT A MISTAKE

01:01:30.061 --> 01:01:31.521
You have 30 seconds left.

01:01:32.647 --> 01:01:33.690
This is frustrating.

01:01:33.773 --> 01:01:36.151
I don't see
any offense options for Myeong-su.

01:01:36.401 --> 01:01:38.069
Song Myeong-su will now take his turn.

01:01:38.153 --> 01:01:39.863
Lee Seung-hyeon will now take his turn.

01:01:39.946 --> 01:01:41.781
Song Myeong-su will now take his turn.

01:01:42.073 --> 01:01:44.075
Lee Seung-hyeon will now take his turn.

01:01:44.409 --> 01:01:45.952
Song Myeong-su will now take his turn.

01:01:46.036 --> 01:01:48.038
I was forced to be on defense,

01:01:48.121 --> 01:01:51.708
so I kept thinking about ways
to turn the tables.

01:02:02.552 --> 01:02:05.430
Isn't that cell indefensible?
You can't place one here.

01:02:05.764 --> 01:02:09.267
Lee Seung-hyeon just built
a four-cell block.

01:02:09.351 --> 01:02:14.105
As a piece cannot be placed
on its one-cell side without a perch,

01:02:14.189 --> 01:02:17.859
Myeong-su cannot place
a new piece in the highlighted spot.

01:02:19.277 --> 01:02:21.404
He can't do anything
about that lower right corner.

01:02:22.280 --> 01:02:24.866
Since I couldn't see
a suitable move for defense...

01:02:26.993 --> 01:02:29.454
- An attack with a four-cell block.
- So that's his next move.

01:02:29.663 --> 01:02:32.290
- That calls for defense.
- Of course.

01:02:36.211 --> 01:02:38.046
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE'S 5-CELL BLOCK

01:02:38.129 --> 01:02:41.258
Oh, I didn't realize
he could cap it off with that piece.

01:02:41.591 --> 01:02:43.176
That never occurred to me.

01:02:51.351 --> 01:02:52.769
It's 2 to 0 now.

01:02:54.646 --> 01:02:55.855
That was fire.

01:02:55.939 --> 01:02:58.358
- Props to him.
- That never crossed my mind.

01:02:58.608 --> 01:03:03.071
Team SNU in Medicine's Lee Seung-hyeon
won Round 2 of Block Connect Five.

01:03:03.154 --> 01:03:07.242
I kept telling myself
I shouldn't miss Myeong-su's mistake.

01:03:07.325 --> 01:03:10.120
That mindset probably gave me the victory.

01:03:10.495 --> 01:03:12.455
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE: 2
TEAM SNU IN STEM: 0

01:03:12.539 --> 01:03:15.583
He beat the second player's disadvantage.
Kudos, Seung-hyeon.

01:03:15.959 --> 01:03:17.002
Well done.

01:03:17.252 --> 01:03:18.753
My bad. I didn't catch that.

01:03:18.837 --> 01:03:19.921
I missed it.

01:03:20.005 --> 01:03:23.258
There was no stopping his final move.

01:03:23.758 --> 01:03:25.885
I felt terrible for my teammates

01:03:25.969 --> 01:03:29.180
for adding to the pressure
with another defeat.

01:03:29.556 --> 01:03:31.016
- Going first?
- What?

01:03:31.099 --> 01:03:33.226
- You'll go first, right?
- Of course.

01:03:33.310 --> 01:03:34.686
Win for us, Gang-hyeon.

01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:36.730
All right.

01:03:36.813 --> 01:03:41.776
The two remaining players are solid.
It's Mr. Chess and Mr. Han Jong-yun.

01:03:41.860 --> 01:03:44.612
Anything can happen in Deathmatches.

01:03:44.696 --> 01:03:46.823
Maybe they reserved their best players.

01:03:46.906 --> 01:03:52.037
They could study the opponents' tactics
and crush them in the later rounds.

01:03:52.120 --> 01:03:54.456
Are we hoping to see
Jong-yun on a rampage?

01:03:54.998 --> 01:03:58.710
Both teams, please decide
on who will compete in Round 3.

01:03:59.210 --> 01:04:02.589
My victory would complete
a 3-0 clean sweep for my team,

01:04:02.672 --> 01:04:05.133
so I was determined to win.

01:04:05.633 --> 01:04:08.511
I had to win to keep my team in the game,

01:04:08.595 --> 01:04:10.722
so I felt more driven to concentrate.

01:04:10.805 --> 01:04:12.098
Please come to the stage.

01:04:12.766 --> 01:04:14.351
- Hello.
- Hello.

01:04:17.645 --> 01:04:20.106
Team SNU in Medicine won
both rounds so far.

01:04:20.190 --> 01:04:21.024
You're right.

01:04:21.107 --> 01:04:23.193
This round could decide the match.

01:04:23.276 --> 01:04:24.736
He's got to step up his game.

01:04:25.528 --> 01:04:29.741
We all knew how brilliant Gang-hyeon is,
so I felt certain he would get us the win.

01:04:30.200 --> 01:04:31.993
Because my team had done so well,

01:04:32.077 --> 01:04:35.246
I expected to see
an overwhelming clean sweep.

01:04:35.330 --> 01:04:40.251
As Team SNU in STEM lost Round 2,
their player will decide who goes first.

01:04:40.335 --> 01:04:41.711
I'll go first.

01:04:43.713 --> 01:04:45.006
Please place a piece.

01:04:50.512 --> 01:04:51.971
Going for the center again.

01:04:52.055 --> 01:04:53.556
I bet Seo-yeon has a counter.

01:04:54.099 --> 01:04:55.892
You have 30 seconds left.

01:05:06.236 --> 01:05:08.947
HAN SEO-YEON'S DEFENSE

01:05:10.615 --> 01:05:12.409
I say Seo-yeon has a solid game plan,

01:05:12.492 --> 01:05:14.744
and Gang-hyeon adapts his
to counter her moves.

01:05:14.828 --> 01:05:17.414
Adaptability is
every STEM student's middle name.

01:05:25.505 --> 01:05:29.509
It's all about rearranging pieces now
since they don't have any good openings.

01:05:29.592 --> 01:05:32.804
The more I watch the game,
the more important the second layer seems.

01:05:38.977 --> 01:05:41.396
She has to defend that spot.

01:05:46.359 --> 01:05:48.778
All pieces have been placed.

01:05:49.737 --> 01:05:51.489
Good, that's our only option.

01:05:51.781 --> 01:05:54.742
GANG-HYEON TURNS A PIECE UPRIGHT

01:05:54.826 --> 01:05:56.619
Things are getting heated
for the second layer.

01:05:56.703 --> 01:05:58.455
Nothing stands out to me.

01:05:58.538 --> 01:06:00.331
I don't see anything, either.

01:06:03.751 --> 01:06:06.171
She has to turn a piece.
There's no other choice.

01:06:06.254 --> 01:06:07.881
That's her only option.

01:06:07.964 --> 01:06:09.674
She has to keep turning pieces.

01:06:13.011 --> 01:06:17.015
Nothing strikes me as a compelling move,
but I feel hesitant to comment.

01:06:17.098 --> 01:06:19.184
What if one move turns out to be pivotal?

01:06:19.267 --> 01:06:22.770
I think you need to look five moves ahead
before reaching a decision.

01:06:39.204 --> 01:06:41.498
I did consider making a change first,

01:06:41.581 --> 01:06:44.959
but I couldn't risk losing,
so I opted for a conservative approach.

01:06:46.377 --> 01:06:47.712
He made the right choice.

01:06:47.795 --> 01:06:49.255
He has to if he wants to win.

01:06:49.339 --> 01:06:51.132
If he loses, he's going home.

01:06:51.216 --> 01:06:53.510
This could be it for his team.
He has to win.

01:06:56.888 --> 01:06:59.265
- Both are being cautious.
- It's a Deathmatch.

01:06:59.349 --> 01:07:01.976
We were just as cautious
in our Deathmatch.

01:07:02.060 --> 01:07:04.604
She can keep at it
and wait for him to mess up.

01:07:04.687 --> 01:07:06.439
- She can strike then.
- Sure.

01:07:06.523 --> 01:07:09.526
She's not moving any of the pieces
she placed on top of Gang-hyeon's.

01:07:13.696 --> 01:07:15.573
We can't afford to lose this time.

01:07:16.491 --> 01:07:20.370
It didn't seem like I could win
with the endless deadlock.

01:07:20.453 --> 01:07:22.580
So I decided to break it with a surprise.

01:07:22.997 --> 01:07:24.123
He's trying something.

01:07:29.963 --> 01:07:31.673
Gang-hyeon took a gamble.

01:07:41.891 --> 01:07:45.019
She can move the piece far up the board.
He can't try anything there.

01:07:45.103 --> 01:07:48.314
- You're right.
- See? She's going to win in two turns.

01:07:48.648 --> 01:07:52.819
If Seo-yeon moves the highlighted piece
as shown on screen

01:07:52.902 --> 01:07:55.196
and lays the next piece flat
on her next turn,

01:07:55.280 --> 01:07:58.116
she can complete her five-cell block.

01:07:58.449 --> 01:08:01.244
- Come on.
- Please catch that.

01:08:01.327 --> 01:08:03.621
- Come on, girl.
- You have five seconds left.

01:08:08.876 --> 01:08:09.961
She saw it.

01:08:11.296 --> 01:08:12.171
There we go.

01:08:23.600 --> 01:08:24.976
TEAM SNU IN STEM'S 5-CELL BLOCK

01:08:25.768 --> 01:08:27.895
I felt a rush of relief.

01:08:28.313 --> 01:08:32.483
Actually, I left the center open
at one point.

01:08:32.567 --> 01:08:34.861
HAN SEO-YEON CLAIMED THE CENTER

01:08:34.944 --> 01:08:38.698
And she never moved that piece afterward.

01:08:39.866 --> 01:08:43.995
I thought I had to reclaim it to win,

01:08:45.038 --> 01:08:46.873
so I lured her into taking it away.

01:08:46.956 --> 01:08:48.666
Gang-hyeon took a gamble.

01:08:48.750 --> 01:08:49.834
HIS PLAN WORKED

01:08:49.917 --> 01:08:53.921
When my trick worked,
I felt convinced I could win.

01:08:54.005 --> 01:08:56.132
KIM GANG-HYEON TOOK THE CENTER RIGHT AWAY

01:08:57.008 --> 01:09:00.219
Team SNU in STEM's Kim Gang-hyeon
completed a five-cell block.

01:09:00.303 --> 01:09:02.221
Only he could've pulled off
that masterstroke.

01:09:05.475 --> 01:09:07.644
As expected from the chess master.

01:09:07.727 --> 01:09:09.270
How clever.

01:09:09.479 --> 01:09:13.941
Team SNU in STEM's Kim Gang-hyeon
won Round 3 of Block Connect Five.

01:09:17.779 --> 01:09:19.405
We'll have to prime you for Round 5.

01:09:19.489 --> 01:09:21.866
- Get ready for another round.
- Of course.

01:09:22.700 --> 01:09:23.660
It's going as I planned.

01:09:23.743 --> 01:09:26.412
Older members covering
for the younger members.

01:09:26.621 --> 01:09:29.457
- I'm so sorry for missing the final move.
- It's okay.

01:09:30.375 --> 01:09:31.834
I was grateful that I won.

01:09:32.085 --> 01:09:35.880
I hoped Jong-yun would win Round 4
so I could secure our survival in Round 5.

01:09:36.381 --> 01:09:37.840
I messed up.

01:09:38.299 --> 01:09:40.885
I got so caught up
in looking for possible attacks

01:09:40.968 --> 01:09:43.012
that I missed the implication
of Gang-hyeon's move.

01:09:43.096 --> 01:09:44.722
I was very disappointed.

01:09:45.098 --> 01:09:48.476
We'll now begin Round 4
of the Deathmatch, Block Connect Five.

01:09:49.143 --> 01:09:51.896
Players competing in Round 4
are Team SNU in STEM's Han Jong-yun

01:09:51.979 --> 01:09:54.691
and Team SNU in Medicine's Kim Min-seok.

01:09:54.774 --> 01:09:56.025
Please come to the stage.

01:09:59.779 --> 01:10:03.950
As Team SNU in Medicine lost Round 4,
their player will decide who goes first.

01:10:04.242 --> 01:10:05.660
I'll go first.

01:10:06.244 --> 01:10:08.996
Team SNU in Medicine's Kim Min-seok
will go first.

01:10:09.080 --> 01:10:10.289
Please place your piece.

01:10:13.918 --> 01:10:16.713
- He needs to seal that spot.
- Yeah, then we're good.

01:10:20.842 --> 01:10:22.260
Okay, so far, so good.

01:10:31.811 --> 01:10:33.020
It's over, isn't it?

01:10:33.104 --> 01:10:34.772
You bet. He's unstoppable now.

01:10:35.064 --> 01:10:36.607
He wins with a block over there.

01:10:36.691 --> 01:10:37.900
Oh, it's over.

01:10:37.984 --> 01:10:39.861
With a block here,

01:10:39.944 --> 01:10:42.280
BECAUSE OF THE 4-CELL BLOCK
it's over.

01:10:42.572 --> 01:10:46.617
Suppose that Jong-yun built
a four-cell block in this turn.

01:10:46.701 --> 01:10:49.996
If Min-seok places a piece
flat on the board for defense,

01:10:50.079 --> 01:10:53.499
Jong-yun can layer a piece over it
and complete his five-cell block.

01:10:53.583 --> 01:10:59.297
This is identical to the winning move
Min-seo used in Round 1.

01:10:59.380 --> 01:11:02.341
JONG-YUN USED
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE'S TACTIC AGAINST THEM

01:11:05.428 --> 01:11:08.598
TEAM SNU IN STEM'S 4-CELL BLOCK

01:11:13.269 --> 01:11:15.980
Wow, we're getting the fifth round.

01:11:22.820 --> 01:11:25.907
That was dynamite.

01:11:26.407 --> 01:11:28.242
I thought, "What a relief. I won."

01:11:29.035 --> 01:11:32.288
Things were literally falling into place.

01:11:36.501 --> 01:11:38.795
They can use this to finish up
before we turn our pieces.

01:11:38.878 --> 01:11:40.421
Let's say they tried this.

01:11:40.505 --> 01:11:41.714
PREPARING FOR EVERY POSSIBILITY

01:11:41.798 --> 01:11:43.633
- Right.
- How's this for defense?

01:11:44.091 --> 01:11:45.802
- I see. A wall works.
- Right?

01:11:45.885 --> 01:11:47.136
We can just build a wall.

01:11:47.220 --> 01:11:50.515
When it comes to the game plans
as the first player...

01:11:50.598 --> 01:11:53.935
Unless our opponent chose
the best move ten times in a row,

01:11:54.018 --> 01:11:56.854
we had a surefire way to defeat them.

01:11:56.938 --> 01:11:59.440
I knew we wouldn't lose when going first.

01:12:00.358 --> 01:12:02.235
- He needs to build a wall.
- Exactly.

01:12:02.318 --> 01:12:04.153
He needs that wall now.

01:12:07.323 --> 01:12:09.075
- What's this?
- That's insane.

01:12:09.158 --> 01:12:11.118
I can't believe it.

01:12:11.202 --> 01:12:12.829
This was the sole viable move.

01:12:12.912 --> 01:12:14.914
He survived that. He's not going down.

01:12:14.997 --> 01:12:18.167
- So that's one way to defend it.
- Looks that way.

01:12:18.251 --> 01:12:20.169
There we go.

01:12:20.253 --> 01:12:22.046
Things are going as we practiced.

01:12:22.129 --> 01:12:23.756
So far, so good.

01:12:24.465 --> 01:12:27.426
Team SNU in STEM's Han Jong-yun
will now take his turn.

01:12:35.768 --> 01:12:37.395
You have 30 seconds left.

01:12:44.610 --> 01:12:47.321
He's basically declaring
that he will turn this next.

01:12:47.405 --> 01:12:48.447
He has to turn this.

01:12:48.531 --> 01:12:50.199
JONG-YUN'S SOLE MEANS OF DEFENSE

01:12:50.283 --> 01:12:51.534
He can't just yet.

01:12:51.617 --> 01:12:52.994
He can't turn his piece.

01:12:53.077 --> 01:12:54.495
- He can't.
- Right.

01:12:54.745 --> 01:12:57.331
He hasn't placed all five pieces yet.

01:12:57.582 --> 01:13:00.167
1 PIECE STILL REMAINS

01:13:00.251 --> 01:13:02.545
Excellent use
of the first-player advantage.

01:13:02.628 --> 01:13:04.088
Min-seok did a great job.

01:13:04.171 --> 01:13:06.632
The first player moves a piece first, too.

01:13:07.049 --> 01:13:09.510
Okay, so we have
our four-cell block, right?

01:13:09.844 --> 01:13:12.221
YOU CAN GET A 4-CELL BLOCK
BY ROTATING THE HIGHLIGHTED PIECE

01:13:12.305 --> 01:13:14.932
- If they don't block here...
- What's our next play?

01:13:15.016 --> 01:13:17.059
- Why not place a piece here?
- Good idea.

01:13:17.143 --> 01:13:18.769
- It's over.
- We win.

01:13:18.853 --> 01:13:20.187
Since we start turning first.

01:13:20.271 --> 01:13:22.690
Take advantage
of that first-player premium.

01:13:23.024 --> 01:13:25.318
Guys, we won.
Min-seok can turn a piece first.

01:13:25.568 --> 01:13:29.739
ONCE JONG-YUN PLACES HIS PIECE,
MIN-SEOK CAN COMPLETE A 5-CELL BLOCK

01:13:33.701 --> 01:13:34.744
I realized I won.

01:13:34.827 --> 01:13:36.203
I felt relieved

01:13:36.287 --> 01:13:40.124
and glad that I managed the game well
according to our strategy.

01:13:40.207 --> 01:13:41.667
You have ten seconds left.

01:13:41.751 --> 01:13:43.836
HAN JONG-YUN PLACES HIS FINAL PIECE

01:13:43.920 --> 01:13:46.464
Team SNU in Medicine's Kim Min-seok
will now take his turn.

01:13:53.429 --> 01:13:57.308
Team SNU in Medicine's Kim Min-seok
completed a five-cell block.

01:13:57.391 --> 01:14:01.520
TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE'S 5-CELL BLOCK

01:14:04.941 --> 01:14:07.193
I messed up big time.

01:14:12.740 --> 01:14:15.368
- That was amazing.
- We might not have survived this.

01:14:15.451 --> 01:14:17.495
The med guys mastered strategies
for going first.

01:14:17.578 --> 01:14:19.038
They had it in the bag.

01:14:19.580 --> 01:14:23.668
Team SNU in Medicine's Kim Min-seok
won Round 4 of Block Connect Five.

01:14:28.381 --> 01:14:29.298
Good job.

01:14:29.799 --> 01:14:30.633
Well done.

01:14:30.716 --> 01:14:32.176
You don't seem happy at all.

01:14:32.510 --> 01:14:35.012
As a fellow SNU student,
I felt bad for the STEM team.

01:14:37.223 --> 01:14:38.557
I guess that was a killer.

01:14:38.641 --> 01:14:41.102
The initial move they stuck with.

01:14:42.770 --> 01:14:44.647
We didn't see it coming, either.

01:14:44.730 --> 01:14:47.066
We thought you were going to win.

01:14:48.734 --> 01:14:53.364
I felt so terrible for my team.

01:14:54.490 --> 01:14:57.785
I couldn't help blaming myself.

01:14:58.953 --> 01:15:01.163
I couldn't quite believe...

01:15:03.332 --> 01:15:05.292
that our journey came to an end.

01:15:07.878 --> 01:15:12.091
That concludes the Deathmatch,
Block Connect Five.

01:15:12.800 --> 01:15:16.387
The third team to be eliminated
from Elite League Season 3 is

01:15:17.096 --> 01:15:19.432
Team SNU in STEM.

01:15:20.641 --> 01:15:24.520
Team SNU in STEM, please exit the grounds.

01:15:26.647 --> 01:15:29.400
Defeat them all in our place.

01:15:29.483 --> 01:15:30.401
Good job, guys.

01:15:34.405 --> 01:15:36.323
I planned on surviving
with Gang-hyeon as our MVP.

01:15:36.407 --> 01:15:38.492
You did your part, but we didn't.

01:15:38.576 --> 01:15:41.078
I felt so sure we won Round 4.

01:15:47.668 --> 01:15:48.961
My heart started racing.

01:15:49.462 --> 01:15:51.589
Since the show's name is "Elite League,"

01:15:51.672 --> 01:15:53.632
I braced myself
like an athlete in a competition.

01:15:53.716 --> 01:15:55.051
I'll log my tile set.

01:15:55.760 --> 01:15:57.219
That was how I felt going in.

01:16:01.974 --> 01:16:03.893
The whole experience was closer

01:16:03.976 --> 01:16:06.145
to a celebration
rather than a competition.

01:16:06.687 --> 01:16:08.105
I was so happy here.

01:16:08.564 --> 01:16:11.192
Honestly speaking,
I expected a better outcome.

01:16:11.275 --> 01:16:13.986
I'm sad because it seems like
my mistake cost my team's survival.

01:16:14.070 --> 01:16:18.240
While we didn't get to be the champions,
we made invaluable friends on the show.

01:16:18.324 --> 01:16:19.366
That was amazing.

01:16:19.450 --> 01:16:21.243
- He delivered!
- Oh, man.

01:16:21.327 --> 01:16:22.787
I'm getting a dopamine rush.

01:16:23.829 --> 01:16:27.666
I'd like to say I have no regrets
because I gave it my all.

01:16:29.960 --> 01:16:32.463
I'll miss everything from the show.

01:16:33.130 --> 01:16:35.466
It's a shame we didn't get to go higher.

01:16:39.053 --> 01:16:43.516
Still, my teammates and I made
great memories during the last four days.

01:16:44.266 --> 01:16:45.601
I'm glad for that.

01:16:45.684 --> 01:16:51.023
I'd like to thank the other teams
for the amazing and fun experience.

01:16:51.107 --> 01:16:52.566
I loved it.

01:16:53.067 --> 01:16:54.068
Are you nervous?

01:16:54.401 --> 01:16:55.653
I'm controlling it.

01:16:55.903 --> 01:16:58.572
I've never been
in a competition like this.

01:16:59.532 --> 01:17:05.371
STEM Division's Ace player is
Team SNU's Song Myeong-su.

01:17:05.788 --> 01:17:09.917
I had fun playing so many different games
with my teammates.

01:17:10.960 --> 01:17:14.713
I hope we can still be great friends
back on campus.

01:17:15.339 --> 01:17:16.507
That was hilarious.

01:17:16.841 --> 01:17:18.467
Lastly,

01:17:18.551 --> 01:17:21.470
we have Team KAIST
representing all STEM students.

01:17:21.554 --> 01:17:23.639
I'll keep rooting for them until the end.

01:17:23.722 --> 01:17:26.350
NO GOOD WISHES FOR TEAM SNU IN MEDICINE,
YOUR FELLOW SNU STUDENTS?

01:17:26.684 --> 01:17:28.352
Good luck, Team SNU in Medicine!

01:17:32.690 --> 01:17:36.193
We wanted to say goodbye
to Team KAIST at the very least.

01:17:37.069 --> 01:17:39.155
Did you hear us cheering for you?

01:17:39.238 --> 01:17:40.781
- We felt it.
- Good.

01:17:49.915 --> 01:17:54.128
The surviving three teams,
please head to your base camps.

01:17:54.211 --> 01:17:55.921
What's this about, anyway?

01:17:56.005 --> 01:17:57.673
What now?

01:17:59.925 --> 01:18:01.427
- What have we got here?
- What on earth?

01:18:01.594 --> 01:18:03.095
SPECIAL MEAL TO BOOST
THE SEMIFINALISTS' STAMINA

01:18:03.179 --> 01:18:05.097
They prepared extra healthy food for us.

01:18:05.306 --> 01:18:06.765
Guys, look at this.

01:18:06.974 --> 01:18:09.685
- These are meal kits.
- "Braised abalone and oxtail"?

01:18:09.894 --> 01:18:12.313
"I would've gotten into SNU
if I'd eaten this before my CSAT."

01:18:12.396 --> 01:18:14.315
That's possible. This is super healthy.

01:18:17.318 --> 01:18:18.569
Let's dig in.

01:18:18.903 --> 01:18:21.071
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

01:18:21.155 --> 01:18:23.073
- Braised oxtail.
- I love this.

01:18:23.157 --> 01:18:25.242
I've never tried this before.

01:18:25.326 --> 01:18:26.452
It's your first-ever oxtail.

01:18:26.535 --> 01:18:28.913
FIRST BITE OF BRAISED OXTAIL

01:18:34.501 --> 01:18:36.128
It's great.

01:18:36.670 --> 01:18:38.297
I can't wait to try the meat.

01:18:38.631 --> 01:18:39.632
Seriously...

01:18:41.091 --> 01:18:43.010
- It's unbelievable.
- They look tasty.

01:18:43.093 --> 01:18:44.929
I can't believe these are meal kits.

01:18:45.512 --> 01:18:47.056
Let me try the abalone.

01:18:47.139 --> 01:18:48.349
Go ahead.

01:18:48.432 --> 01:18:49.808
It's huge.

01:18:50.059 --> 01:18:52.728
- It's gigantic.
- It's gigantic.

01:18:52.811 --> 01:18:53.646
Jinx.

01:18:58.567 --> 01:19:01.195
It's crazy. The abalone tastes wonderful.

01:19:01.445 --> 01:19:02.988
I'll try the perilla oil noodles.

01:19:03.822 --> 01:19:06.617
- The perilla oil is so aromatic.
- It's insanely good.

01:19:06.700 --> 01:19:09.286
We need good fats
for our brains to function faster.

01:19:09.370 --> 01:19:10.537
Foodie YouTubers always do this.

01:19:15.125 --> 01:19:16.126
- He's enjoying it.
- Indeed.

01:19:16.752 --> 01:19:17.962
It's actually good, though.

01:19:18.045 --> 01:19:20.005
It's so good.

01:19:20.756 --> 01:19:22.633
I should ask my mom to get me these.

01:19:22.967 --> 01:19:25.094
Buy it yourself with the prize money.

01:19:26.470 --> 01:19:28.430
There's no need to go to your mother.

01:19:29.640 --> 01:19:30.599
I'll do as you say.

01:19:31.767 --> 01:19:34.353
The main match for the semifinal is

01:19:34.436 --> 01:19:36.230
Secret Student Club.

01:19:36.313 --> 01:19:37.439
- What?
- A reasoning game?

01:19:37.523 --> 01:19:39.191
Similar to Find My Personality Type
from Season 1?

01:19:39.275 --> 01:19:40.276
Probably.

01:19:40.359 --> 01:19:42.695
Please go to the Club Rooms.

01:19:42.778 --> 01:19:45.155
The whole setup makes me feel
like I'm on campus.

01:19:45.239 --> 01:19:46.365
Will we get a talent show?

01:19:46.448 --> 01:19:48.242
- I'll dance if it's an option.
- Really?

01:19:49.702 --> 01:19:50.828
Gosh, thank you.

01:19:50.911 --> 01:19:53.163
I'm in a band,
a drama club, and a dance club.

01:19:53.247 --> 01:19:54.206
- Seriously?
- Yes.

01:19:54.290 --> 01:19:55.833
You're the full package.

01:20:03.424 --> 01:20:05.050
Let's wipe out that club's members.

01:20:05.134 --> 01:20:08.971
Please state the club and the rank
of the person whose identity you deduced.

01:20:09.054 --> 01:20:10.055
They are a member of the band.

01:20:10.139 --> 01:20:11.140
What?

01:20:11.515 --> 01:20:12.683
What are they doing?

01:20:12.766 --> 01:20:15.227
We might end up
with Team KAIST on the throne.

01:20:15.311 --> 01:20:18.939
Marking Team SKKU alone
might not be the best course of action.

01:20:19.023 --> 01:20:21.734
